From c96c6e3d09ae5697b58bc630115fd5a56357f5d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:50:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] msearch, scheduler: make d-first sums unambiguous to
 the scheduler

msearch --diag-first writes "dsquare" / "dchunk" / "dsum" records for the
d-first sums and no "sum" record, but its "done" record still covered
them. scheduler.py's Results took every sum in a done range without a
sum record for a searched sum without squares: a d-first sum looked
empty, and a --d-stride sample or a --d-range part looked searched, so
the scheduler would never search the rest of it.

msearch: "dsum" records get "mode":"dfirst" and "complete" (every d of
the sum searched: not a d-range part, a d sample, a truncated or stopped
run), and with --diag-first the "done" record gets "mode":"dfirst" and
diag_first_min_n.

scheduler.py: Results keeps the dsum records apart (results.dsums) and
the magic squares found d-first (results.dmagic, shown by report), out
of the squares / traversal / time fits until the model is taught to use
them; a complete d-first sum counts as covered, an incomplete one (or an
older record without "complete") is cut out of the file's done ranges
(split_range). test_scheduler.py checks both on synthetic records and on
msearch output (complete sums covered, a d-sampled one not).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GSaYLGdzq6d82nBLeSZFgB
